SheetStack shows the documents delivered with a system as an exploded stack of isometric drawing sheets, each sheet drawing in miniature what the document is, its row beside it.

- On the site: a `docs` block with `"look": "sheet-stack"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-sheet-stack.js`), sys-storage "Documents with the loop". Origin: no concept of its own; adapted from the clipped proof sheets of `research/pass9/concepts/compliance.2.v2.png` and the brief's "layers explode apart and settle", in a tactile-object direction.
- Markup: `div.aq-sheet-stack` > `span.__axis` (dashed explode axis), `ol.__rows` of `li.__row(.is-key)` (`span.__slot` > `span.__sheet` aria-hidden svg: miniature, frame, title block with the code; `div.__text`: `p.__code` with `span.__i` index and `span.__k` code, `h3.__t`, `p.__d`), then `p.__more` (the block link as a Button link).
- Fields: `h`, `items [{t, d, key, code, sheet, link, intent}]`, `link`, `link_label`, `intent`, `fold`, `fold_noun`. `sheet`: `calc` (bars past a dashed limit), `register` (a table of tees), `iso` (a P&ID with valves and an instrument), `cert` (a certificate with its seal); default from the DocList code (HYD, DLR, P&ID or ISO, MAT). Codes come from DocList's lookup (`docCode`) unless `code` is set.
- Tokens: `surface-raised` sheets with a `line-strong` edge for thickness (no shadows), `flow` bars and seals, key codes in `flow`.
- Pointing at a row lifts its sheet. Fold: phones only.
- Phones: a small sheet beside each row, axis on the left.

## Motion

Motion: the set arrives as one pile in the middle, then explodes apart, each sheet rising or sinking to its row and settling; the axis draws out from the middle; the miniatures draw on (bars run out past the limit line); each row slides in beside its sheet, its code decoding. Under 5 s; nothing under reduced motion.
